@aoshen02 @hao-aaron Following up on the pending-update inference guard in F2 / #64418 §8. My earlier Muse findings are now covered by #65125 and #49459.

With Qwen3-1.7B on an RTX 4090, using main Python source at `0d9d953d68` with existing nightly native artifacts, I reproduced this in both in-process and multiprocess eager execution: `is_inference_ready()` returns false after starting an update, and after a transfer-metadata failure, but `LLM.generate()` still succeeds. A subsequent complete checkpoint load and successful finish restores readiness. The injected failure happens before any weight data is received; this does not demonstrate partial-write corruption.

I plan to work on enforcing the pending state at the Engine/Core boundary, including target/draft failure recovery and queued-request handling. Please let me know if there is already an implementation in progress so I can align with it.
